      <item>
        <title>Failed load Kernel Modules</title>
        <dc:creator><![CDATA[spartack]]></dc:creator>
        <description><![CDATA[
            <p>That’s true, I’m actively trying to use KDE with kicksecure, is the best DE nowadays.<br>
Could you try the following:</p>
<ol>
<li>Go to <code>/usr/lib/modules-load.d/</code> and <code>/etc/modules-load.d/</code></li>
<li>There should be all the modules loaded by the system</li>
<li>Make a <code>sudo modprobe &lt;module&gt; &lt;module&gt;</code>…</li>
</ol>
<p>It should tell you which module is failing, and it should be into <code>/lib/modules/$(uname -r)/ </code>to be able to be caught by the kernel on boot.</p>
          <p><a href="https://forums.kicksecure.com/t/failed-load-kernel-modules/1777/7">Read full topic</a></p>
        ]]></description>
